From 14046e10fb9216133a2c1784619be2b6e9bda0e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: a1go3 <116062404+a1go3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:12:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tls): split the ClientHello over several TLS records

Provider filters freeze a server port after reading a whole ClientHello from the first TLS record, while a hello spread over records passes and servers reassemble it. VLESS gains a tls-fragment option (enable, packets: tlshello, length, interval in ms, ranges allowed) that re-frames only the first handshake record, leaving the handshake bytes, the transcript and the REALITY session ID as they are. REALITY profiles split by default with Xray's values, 100-200 bytes a record written 1 ms apart, since subscriptions carry no fragment settings; tls-fragment with enable: false turns it off.
